# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 6.4
HD("6.4 When increased model complexity reduces reliability", 2)
l0, l2, l3, l4 = GM[0]["models"], GM[2]["models"], GM[3]["models"], GM[4]["models"]
P("The results demonstrate that increased spatial-model complexity does not necessarily improve safety-critical decision reliability. In the matched model the lateral tracker with three parallel passes has a false clearance of %s%% against %s%% for the one-dimensional continuity filter and %s%% for per-segment fusion (version 1.1 experiment, Table 7), and it keeps false alarms low when utilities shift sideways. "
  "Under structural mismatch involving a parallel utility, or a parallel utility and a branch, the continuity-aware model with lateral tracking has a false clearance of %s%% and %s%%, against %s%% and %s%% for the simpler one-dimensional filter and %s%% and %s%% for per-segment fusion. "
  "The same reversal is found in the present experiment with the health-aware lateral policies, whose conditional risk rises from %s%% (P2, matched) to %s%% (parallel) and %s%% (parallel and branch), against %s%% and %s%% for the 1D framework. "
  "A model with abrupt bends alone (L2) does not cause it (%s%% against %s%% for the matched case). The lateral tracker attributes the returns of the parallel line to the best-fitting offset, takes the line for the target, and clears the excavation footprint on which the real utility lies; the one-pass filters keep calling the footprint occupied whenever they see a return and are safe in this respect only because they cannot tell the lines apart. "
  "A model that is more capable when its assumptions hold can therefore be the less reliable model when they do not: it becomes overconfident when its assumed spatial structure does not represent the network, and the calibration gap of Section 6.2 shows the size of that overconfidence. "
  "Consequently, reliability assessment must evaluate not only performance under nominal conditions but also the possibility that the model’s own assumptions become a source of unsafe decisions. These findings motivate explicit model-mismatch diagnostics, conservative abstention and independent verification where structural uncertainty cannot be resolved." % (
      pc(l0["proposed_3pass"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]), pc(l0["continuity_1d"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]), pc(l0["fusion"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]),
      pc(l3["proposed_3pass"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]), pc(l4["proposed_3pass"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]), pc(l3["continuity_1d"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]), pc(l4["continuity_1d"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]), pc(l3["fusion"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]), pc(l4["fusion"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]),
      q("baseline", "P2"), q("G3_parallel", "P2"), q("G4_parallel_branch", "P2"), q("G3_parallel", "B2"), q("G4_parallel_branch", "B2"), pc(l2["proposed_3pass"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0]), pc(l0["proposed_3pass"]["metrics"]["false_clearance"][0])), align="justify")
